So my reading: proposals 1 and 7, which split the requirement by who acts, conflict with the rule "A requirement is not split into pieces." I should reject the split. But there's nuance: proposal 1's underlying concern is real — the current wording "an ambiguous match is treated as certain, or a candidate not built is not named" mixes tool and agent in one clause. The rule says keep the requirement whole. So accept with wording: keep it as one Fails-if line but make each obligation clear. Actually, hmm.

