Guiding principle (my reading + items): A requirement must be whole, clear, and enforceable by the tool it binds, and must not demand of people (the agent) what only structure (the tool) can guarantee. State what the tool establishes and the limit when it cannot. Reject clauses that add no enforceable difference or that split the requirement.

