Proposed final A2:

**A2 The call chain through one place.** Given code or a description, the tool locates the place and returns its caller and callee chains, counted in levels from the place; the place is level 0, and each call link adds one level. The user sets the depth each way; when the user does not, it is six. Every link the type checker establishes within the selected depth is included regardless of traversal order; reaching a function again does not lose a link reachable through a shorter path. When more than one place matches, the tool flags the match as ambiguous and lists every candidate with its location; the agent picks the place that fits the question best, builds its chain, and names every other candidate it did not build. Each link names the body that holds the call and gives its kind and location. A body written straight into a call is a place of its own or a stated limit; it is never shown as a call by the function that surrounds it. A function reached twice is shown once, with a reference back.
**Fails if:** any of these happens:
- a place the question names is not found;
- an ambiguous match is not flagged, a matching candidate is not listed with its location, an ambiguous match is treated as certain, or a candidate the agent did not build is not named;
- a link the type checker establishes within the depth is missing, or a shown link contradicts the code (including a link credited to a function that does not hold the call);
- a link lacks its kind or location;
- a function reached twice is shown twice.

