**A2 The call chain through one place.** Given code or a description, the tool locates the place and returns its caller and callee chains, counted in levels from the place; the place is level 0, and each call link adds one level. The user sets the depth each way; when the user does not, it is six. Every link the type checker establishes within the selected depth is included regardless of traversal order, and reaching a function again does not lose a link reachable through a shorter path. When more than one place matches, the tool flags the match as ambiguous and lists every matching candidate with its location; the agent picks the place that fits the question best, builds its chain, and names every other candidate it did not build. Each link names the body that holds the call and gives its kind and location. A body written straight into a call is a place of its own or a stated limit; it is never shown as a call by the function that surrounds it. A function reached twice is shown once, with a reference back.
