"Costs and risks": each with its item.
- Proposal 3 (my #2/#16): the requirement now says the unheld body is its own place; the tool's `belongsTo` presently folds its calls into the surrounding function for `callees`, so the tool must change, and existing answers for surrounding functions will change. (my reading of `commands.ts` `calleesOf` + `belongsTo`).
- Proposal 4 (my #11, quoted "pay for it"?): depth as shortest distance costs a rework of chain traversal (track remaining depth per function) and can make a chain wider; without it, A2's missing-link line stays failed on the real CLI (confirmed NOT MET on shorter-route-down/up).
- "the type checker establishes" for links (my #11): a check and the tool could still share one reading if the type checker's answer is the tool's own; the cost is a check that is only as independent as the checker.
- A5 "unrelated" (my #16): "unrelated" has no measurable boundary; a strict reading can punish a legitimate answer (the query header, a seen limit's ref), and a loose reading lets a dump pass.
- A5 form + content boundary (my #4): the same missing limit or extra table may now fail A5 and L1/A1 at once; a reader may count one fault three times.
- Splitting rejected (my #3): the agent's half stays inside A2/A5, so the evaluator still reports part of A2/A5 NOT CHECKED; the cost is a report that cannot show the tool's part alone.
- Merging 5/6/8/9 into one A5 line (my #14): fewer, denser clauses; a reader must hold the whole line.

"How we would know I was right":
- A test: the four shorter-route cases (down, down-reversed, up, up-reversed) all MET on the real CLI, and the tail link at the depth-three level appears through the shorter route regardless of source order (proposal 4).
- A test: `callers` on an unheld generator body returns `from` = the body's own location, never the surrounding function's, and `callees` on the surrounding function no longer lists calls made inside the unheld body (proposal 3).
- A test: a default-text answer that carries the right answer plus an unrelated definition or a whole map fails A5, and a JSON answer that carries an unrelated top-level section fails A5 (proposals 5/8/9).
- A test: an answer with a silent cap and no limit fails A5; an answer that carries the interface-required limit passes (proposal 6).
- An observable: the A5 line's wording lists the same failures the strengthened cases (A5-exact-callees, A5-default-text, A5-exact-not-found, A5-exact-depth-stop) each charge; no clause the cases check is missing from the wording, and no clause the wording adds is unchecked.

