**A5 One question, one answer.** A specific question gets that whole answer, with its evidence and its limits, in the form the command answers in — the default text or JSON — and not a whole-map dump. Where the answer stops short — a cap, a sample, a first page — it carries the limit that says so. A limit the interface requires for that command is part of the answer. The answer contains the requested result, its supporting evidence, its applicable limits and the matching places needed to resolve an ambiguity; it excludes unrelated definitions, links, flows and tables, whether they appear in another section or inside the requested payload, in JSON and in the default text. A whole map is produced only when the user asks for a module map; no command other than a module map returns map content.
**Fails if:** an answer comes inside a dump or with unasked sections; lacks its evidence, its limits, or the limit that says where it stops short; carries unrelated definitions, links, flows or tables, in another section or inside the requested payload; or a whole map is produced unasked, or a command other than a module map returns map content.

